CODESTREAM TEMPLATE REPOSITORY
==============================

This marker declares that this directory is the framework's own source
repository — not a project built with the framework.

Effect (HARD_RULES rule 22): /onboard and the rule 10 pre-flight abort here.
Do not run /discover, /prototype, /plan, /execute, /steer, or /log in this
directory.

Why: every runtime file under .codestream/ is tracked by git — STATE.json,
BUGS.md, FEATURES.md, DISCOVERY.md, ROADMAP.md, documents/**, and the
append-only archive logs. Running the lifecycle here writes real project state
into those files, which then ships inside every future project that copies this
template. Rule 12 makes the archive logs append-only, so the smell is expensive
to remove afterwards.

Why the repo root and not inside .codestream/: adoption copies .codestream/
wholesale, so a flag inside it would travel downstream and block real projects
instead of this one. Do NOT add this file to the adoption copy list in
README.md, and do NOT copy it into a downstream project.

To validate a framework change end to end: work in a throwaway downstream
project, then push the improvement back with /extract-template.

Overriding (deliberate dogfooding only): state explicitly that you intend to run
the lifecycle in the template repo. The override is session-scoped. If you find
this marker inside a downstream project, it was copied in by mistake — delete it
there; do not weaken the check here.

Helper: scripts/check-framework.py verifies rule 22's invariant (that this
repo's runtime state is still pristine) along with the mirror checks.
